From: mscharged-port contributors
Subject: [PATCH] Allow PE color aperture writes into a multisampled EFB
Upstream-base: d664382f57002fbff143911c81b06b7e7a4b3ab4
Classification: host presentation option (multisampling) support.

0034's PE aperture refused a multisampled EFB. A poke draws a pixel-aligned
rectangle with the clear pipeline found for the render target's own layout,
including its sample count, and such a rectangle covers every sample of each
poked pixel; a later resolve therefore reads exactly the written color. The
original loading bitmap and HOME button writes now also work with Aurora
multisampling. Scaled (non-1x) EFBs remain unsupported. Apply after 0074.
diff --git a/lib/gfx/recording.cpp b/lib/gfx/recording.cpp
index 6931972..03dcc3c 100644
--- a/lib/gfx/recording.cpp
+++ b/lib/gfx/recording.cpp
@@ -917,8 +917,10 @@ void queue_efb_poke(uint16_t x, uint16_t y, uint32_t argb, bool color, bool alph
   // Physical aperture coordinates are not clipped by ordinary GX draw state.
   AURORA_ASSERT(x < target.x && y < target.y,
       "Native PE aperture {},{} is outside qualified EFB {}x{}", x, y, target.x, target.y);
+  // A multisampled EFB takes the poke through the clear pipeline of its own
+  // sample count; the pixel-aligned rectangle covers every sample of each
+  // poked pixel, so a later resolve reads exactly the written color.
   const auto layout = get_render_target_layout();
-  AURORA_ASSERT(layout.sampleCount == 1, "Native multisample PE aperture remains unqualified");
   if (!color && !alpha) return; // Actual independent PE write masks disabled.
   const clear::PipelineConfig config{.clearColor = color, .clearAlpha = alpha, .clearDepth = false};
   const PokeDrawData data{
